{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfAHuzvHgxjZmabfdjcVR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I submitted **index 6** (Sb fraction 0.101). At 0.130%, it had the highest EQE of the five compositions I measured. All 5 EQE measurements were used; none of the 5 XRD measurements were used.\n\n| Index | Sb fraction | EQE (%) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | 0.057 | 0.095 |\n| **6** | **0.101** | **0.130** |\n| 8 | 0.124 | 0.119 |\n| 15 | 0.259 | 0.095 |\n| 24 | 0.516 | 0.079 |\n\n- **Strategy:** the first three measurements were spread across the line. EQE rose toward low Sb, so the last two went on the low-Sb side of index 6.\n- **Where the peak is:** EQE drops on both sides of index 6, so the best composition is probably at an Sb fraction of about 0.06–0.12. The line has 29 compositions and I measured only 5. The unmeasured ones closest to index 6 (indices 2–5 and 7) could still beat it.\n- **Signal size:** all the EQE values are small (below 0.13%) under 2.4 eV light. This fits Y–Sb oxides absorbing only weakly at that photon energy.\n- **XRD:** I skipped it because it wouldn't have changed which compositions I measured for EQE."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":441,"cache_read_input_tokens":6778,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":441},"output_tokens":444,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7cfa5929-25b2-40e8-800c-b0d94b8af863","uuid":"ac0e1df6-a463-4ae3-9991-56a4c8d20b63","timestamp":"2026-09-18T04:42:38.868Z","request_id":"req_011CfAHuzTWKDTo4UUNkQMXi"}
